* THE TOUR: A PLAYLIST RUN DECK (VIEW-1108, #18).
*
* The situations at slow real-time rates, each shot dipping to black at both
* ends; the tour loops.  The demo reel hands over to it when its last shot
* ends.  Card format: data/reels/demo/run.scn.  The shots, their order,
* rates and looks are all ours.
*
REEL ID=TOUR TITLE="TOUR" KIND=PLAYLIST ALIAS=TOUR FADE=0.8 SRC="ours"
*
* Earthrise from ERFIND's Earthrise less 60 s (102:14:03.686 in today's
* kernel; see the demo reel), at 1x, the camera lifting 4 deg.
SHOT SIT=1 NAME="Earthrise" DUR=200 GET=102:14:03.686 RATE=1 FOV=14 ROLL=-3 PITCH=LIN:0,4 FRAME=YES SRC="ours"
*
* Earth approach: the demo reel's law, over 150 s.
SHOT SIT=2 NAME="Earth approach" DUR=150 AT=195:03:06 TTE=0:11600,0.14:6500,0.62:900,1:600 LIMB=0:-11,0.14:-11.6,0.62:-13,1:-6 FOV=60 SRC="ours"
*
* Earth parking orbit at 1:30:00, panning 30 deg.
SHOT SIT=3 NAME="Earth limb" DUR=90 GET=1:30:00 RATE=1 YAW=LIN:-15,15 FRAME=YES SRC="ours"
*
* Transposition and docking: from the docking approach (APPR, 3:20:30) to
* just after docking (DOCK, 3:24:03.1), at 2x.
SHOT SIT=7 NAME="Transposition & docking" DUR=110 GET=APPR RATE=2 FRAME=YES SRC="ours"
*
* The LM's pirouette after undocking, at 2x.
SHOT SIT=4 NAME="LM pirouette" DUR=120 GET=UNDOCK+120 RATE=2 SRC="ours"
*
* The LM descent, from the demo reel's start to 102:45:45, six seconds after
* touchdown (TOUCH, 102:45:39.9).
SHOT SIT=5 NAME="LM descent" DUR=115 GET=102:40:56 TO=102:45:45 FRAME=YES SRC="ours"
*
* The Moon view at touchdown, held, spun once around in longitude with a
* nod in latitude.
SHOT SIT=6 NAME="Moon view — spin to explore" DUR=75 GET=TOUCH RATE=0 YAW=LIN:-180,180 PITCH=SIN:0,14 LABELS=YES FRAME=YES SRC="ours"
*
* The docked stack, a modern addition: orbit it from outside, then look out
* of the CM's left rendezvous window (yaw -4, pitch 21 from the CM station's
* +X: the window's centre seen from the eye, CMINT in src/models.f).
SHOT SIT=8 NAME="Translunar stack - external" DUR=90 GET=PTC+1800 RATE=1 VIEW=EXTERNAL FOV=24 YAW=LIN:120,240 PITCH=HAV:-10,35 FRAME=YES SRC="ours, a modern addition"
SHOT SIT=8 NAME="Translunar stack - CM window" DUR=60 GET=PTC+1890 RATE=1 VIEW=CM YAW=-4 PITCH=21 FRAME=YES SRC="ours, a modern addition"
*
* Apollo 8 Earthrise (24 Dec 1968): from 2 minutes before the photograph
* (PHOTO, 75:48:39.7) at 4x, the Earth rising.  The span is our first guess.
SHOT SIT=9 NAME="Apollo 8 Earthrise" DUR=120 GET=PHOTO-120 RATE=4 FRAME=YES SRC="ours"
